<title>USA: US Mint buys 1,695,000 kg copper at $2.5497/kg.</title>
<headline>US Mint buys 1,695,000 kg copper at $2.5497/kg.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Mint said Wednesday it awarded a contract to Cerro Sales Corp, of New York, for 1,695,000 kilograms of copper at an average $2.5497 per kilogram for use in coinage.</p>
<p>The purchase included 1,619,000 kilograms at $2.5486 per kilogram, 18,144 kilograms at $2.5816 per kilogram, and 57,856 kilograms at $2.5706 per kilogram.</p>
